  - History (`view=history`, answered by the tool from `TeamHistoryService` in `v1/stats`, masked whole, then paged by `historyAnswer` in the tool's reader): a history that fits one page answers whole; a longer one answers its summary and each section's size, and `section` (`versions`, `changeLog`, `recommendations`, `members`) reads a page at a time, cut between records and each page valid JSON on its own, a record past a page coming in parts (`part`). A version record carries only its diff's `added` and `removed`; the diff itself is `section=diff` with `version`, cut on line breaks. `offset` with no section still cuts the old chunks of the whole answer, for a chat mid-read across an update. It holds every recorded version newest first with its diff (`TeamVersionsService`) and figures over EVERY run the ledgers kept, deleted ones included (runs, cost, turns, the CLIs' own worked time, pull-request outcomes — `foldTeamHistory`); the change log; and every recommendation filed about the team with its status (`applied` / `skipped` / `failed` as marked — for an `X-` item, applied means its card was filed — `selected` in an Apply but never marked, `not-selected` when an Apply took others from its card, else `open` while its chat exists and `unanswered` once a new analysis replaced the card before any Apply — never decided, so the guide files it again when the runs still call for it), its estimates (`expectedMinutesSavedPerRun`, `expectedCostSavedPerRunUsd`, `expectedOutcome`), linked to the logged change that carried it out. Offered to any analysis with a team (`analysedTeamOf`): a team analysis, a builder chat, a thread analysis of a team run.
  - Spend (`view=spend`, answered by the tool from `TeamHistoryService.spend`, masked, then paged by `spendAnswer` in the tool's reader; pure fold `foldTeamSpend` in `v1/stats/utils/team-spend-fold.ts`, `NOT_A_TEAM` for a plain chat): every `usage_events` row of every thread row stamped with the team, so archived and deleted runs count whatever the analysis samples, in three windows (all, the last 30 days, the analysed runs) each saying what it covers, and per project, member and model, none capped; past one page those three are read by `section` like view=history's. A turn is filed under the project its folder belongs to (`ProjectRootsService` + `nearestProjectOf`), one row per project; a folder in no project is named by its last segment alone, since these runs can be work the analysis was never started on. A turn's bill is apportioned among input, cache read, cache write and output by its tokens at `AgentAdapter.billingRatesOf`, the catalog's rates with `AdapterListPrice.cacheWriteInputMultiple` where the CLI writes a longer-lived cache than the catalog prices, so the parts sum to the bill (each is then rounded to the cent, so a row's parts can read a cent or two off) whatever tier or delegate money it holds; polled money and a model with no list price are `notSplitUsd`. `largestCacheWrites` names 10 rows and bounds no count.
  - The change log (`team_change_log`, `TeamChangeLogService` in `v1/teams`, teardown-exempt) gets one entry per library write geniro makes on someone's say-so, AFTER the file is written (a failed log write is logged and never refuses the save): an analysis's applied save (`source: 'analysis'`, the Apply's ids and card seq, the items' titles), an approved `propose_team` card (`'builder'` when the chat edits that team — its ids read from the card's summary and reason, which the builder's brief has name them — else `'chat'`, with the user's note), a version restore (`'restore'`), and a lesson the user saved into a member's instructions (`'lesson'`, the source thread as its chat, with the backup). Each carries the team versions it moved between. An editor save is not logged: a version no entry made reads as edited by hand.
  - The recommendation ledger (`team_recommendations`, `RecommendationLedgerService` in `v1/stats`, teardown-exempt) copies every `recommendations` card a team analysis or builder chat files, every Apply selecting from one and every `recommendation_outcome` mark, off `bus.all()`, serialized per chat, with a boot sweep over the chats that still exist; a card is filed once, the first selection stands, and a mark moves forward only by its row's seq. A new analysis deletes the chat it replaces, so this copy is the only record of what was recommended before.
  - Evidence names its `runId` and is checked against that run's snapshot, a run outside the sample against the pin its read made: one this turn has not read is refused, since a citation never pins anything, so no seq past what the agent could read passes. The card carries no timing strip (one run's would pass for the team's); it carries `teamStats` instead (`teamCardStats` in `utils/team-runs-fold.ts` over `ThreadReaderService.foldRuns`, the folds `view=runs` answers from): averages and totals over every analysed run at its own snapshot, each run with its version number (the tool hands `report_recommendations` the stats module's version index, as for `view=runs`), each agent's working time, share, critical path, calls and cost — every per-run figure divided by the runs that measured it — with its models, the longest caller→callee edges with the uncapped edge count, and `population`, so a sample and its savings estimates read against every run the team has. It is measured when the card is filed, never taken from the agent, and read back with `.catch(null)`, so a stats block that no longer parses never makes the card unreadable to Apply, marks or the ledger. `view=team` and `save_team_change` act on the analysis's own slug (`ThreadReaderService.analysedTeamOf`); `view=team runId=…` sets the library against that run's own copy. Every "is this an analysis" check on a row is `utils/analysed-runs.ts` `isAnalysisRun`.
